IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sv71-nouns`
IMPORT `sv71-cross-references`

-- Row il-71. TESTS OF THE CONTROLS: the sound readings kept beside the defects. They pass.
-- Each control shows that the test finds what it looks for where it is there, so that a failing test in sv71-tests-red.l4 is a finding and not a test that cannot succeed.
-- The expected values are written from the quotation lines in sv71-cross-references.l4 and from the printed pages, not copied from the values there.

§ `Tests of the controls`

-- I1 control 1: the word test finds the term when it is there. Paragraph (2) as SH 2190 printed it contains the term, and the pointer test finds it when the named paragraph is that print.
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `paragraph (2) as printed in SH 2190` "ילד"
#ASSERT `the paragraph the pointer names contains the term in marks` `the pointer in paragraph (4), tried against paragraph (2) as SH 2190 printed it`

-- I1 control 2: the words of paragraph (4) as SH 2338 printed it contain the string the first pointer begins with, and both pointers are among them.
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `paragraph (4) as printed in SH 2338` "להגדרה ״ילד״"
#ASSERT all (GIVEN s YIELD CONTAINS (`paragraph (4) as printed in SH 2338`'s `its words`) s) `the two pointers inside paragraph (4)`
#ASSERT `the pointer's words are among the words of the text that holds it` `the pointer in paragraph (4) to paragraph (2)`

-- I1 control 3: paragraph (2) is replaced by SH 2632 and still exists, in contrast with paragraph (3), which the same section deletes.
#ASSERT `the instruction leaves the named paragraph in place` `SH 2632 section 90(1) replaces paragraph (2) of 11(gimel)`
#ASSERT NOT (`the instruction leaves the named paragraph in place` `SH 2632 section 90(2) deletes paragraph (3) of 11(gimel)`)

-- I1 control 4: the instrument that inserted paragraph (4) and the instrument that replaced paragraph (2) are two different issues.
#ASSERT `the two instruments are two different issues` `SH 2338` `SH 2632`

-- I1 limb (b) control: the test that looks for an instruction naming a place finds the places that later instructions do name.
#ASSERT `some instruction in the list names the place` `paragraph 11(gimel)(2)` `the instructions on section 11 issued after SH 2338`
#ASSERT `some instruction in the list names the place` `paragraph 11(gimel)(3)` `the instructions on section 11 issued after SH 2338`
#ASSERT `some instruction in the list names the place` `subsection 11(vav)` `the instructions on section 11 issued after SH 2338`

-- I2 control 1: section 21 is written in 1963 and replaced by section 67 of SH 2024 at that place.
#ASSERT `the phrase written in the text is replaced at that place by a later instruction` `the phrase P` `section 21 as printed in SH 404` `the instructions deposited here that replace or delete words at section 21 or subsection 11(he)`

-- I2 control 2: the words section 67 replaces are the phrase P letter for letter; the phrase occurs in the 1977 print of subsection (ה) and in the 1963 print of section 21.
#ASSERT `SH 2024 section 67 replaces the phrase P in section 21`'s `the words it names` EQUALS LIST `the phrase P`
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `subsection (he) as printed in SH 856` `the phrase P`
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `section 21 as printed in SH 404` `the phrase P`

-- I2 control 3: the 2005 law replaces words of the same kind in the Retirement Age Law with the same replacement string it uses in section 21.
#ASSERT `SH 2024 section 67 replaces the phrase P in section 21`'s `the words it puts` EQUALS `SH 2024 section 84 on the Retirement Age Law`'s `the words it puts`

-- I2 limb (b) control: the test that looks for words an instruction names inside the phrase finds them where they are (the phrase contains these words of its own).
#ASSERT CONTAINS `the phrase P` "פקודת מס הכנסה"
#ASSERT NOT (`no words the instruction names occur inside the phrase` `the phrase P` `SH 2024 section 67 replaces the phrase P in section 21`)
